   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Warts likely • Usually on hands, knees or elbows but can occur anywhere. • Plantar warts on the soles of the feet are thick and hard with black dot/s.",
   "bbox": [
    39.7,
    264.4,
    164.3,
    325.4
   ],
   "key": "p89-0e1e754f"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e28",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• Reassure that warts often resolve spontaneously. • If treatment desired: - Soften wart/s by soaking in warm",
   "bbox": [
    39.7,
    340.7,
    168.7,
    380.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-693fdd95"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e29",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "water for 5 minutes at night and scrub gently with clean nail file. - After drying well, apply",
   "bbox": [
    45.4,
    380.7,
    165.6,
    410.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-2f9d0d94"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e30",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "petroleum jelly to surrounding skin to protect it, then apply salicylic acid 15-30% to wart, and cover with plaster. - Repeat every night and continue",
   "bbox": [
    45.4,
    410.1,
    169.2,
    460.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-9b7b1a43"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e31",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "for a week after wart has come off. • If extensive warts or plantar wart in diabetic, refer.",
   "bbox": [
    39.7,
    460.7,
    167.0,
    500.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-7ff28e58"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e32",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Molluscum contagiosum likely • Test for HIV 124. • Reassure that lesions often resolve spontaneously after years or with ART. • If treatment desired: open molluscum with sterile needle and apply tincture of iodine BP1 to centre of each lesion. • Refer if: - Extensive - Lesions on eyelid - Intolerable and",
   "bbox": [
    185.7,
    311.0,
    268.0,
    482.0
   ],
   "key": "p89-1c5d89bf"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e33",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "not responding to treatment.",
   "bbox": [
    197.0,
    481.8,
    265.6,
    502.0
   ],
   "key": "p89-40a0fea9"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e34",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Kaposi’s sarcoma",
   "bbox": [
    289.9,
    325.9,
    359.3,
    336.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-dd95a789"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e35",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "likely • Lesions vary from isolated lumps to large ulcerating tumours. • May also appear in mouth and on genitals.",
   "bbox": [
    286.0,
    336.7,
    357.5,
    416.9
   ],
   "key": "p89-f0f70fcd"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e36",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• Test for HIV 124. • Refer for biopsy to confirm diagnosis and for further management.",
   "bbox": [
    286.1,
    432.2,
    360.6,
    492.4
   ],
   "key": "p89-5e460721"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e37",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• If not infected, reassure there is no need to treat. • If fluctuant, arrange incision and drainage. If on face, refer instead. • If infected (skin red, warm, painful):",
   "bbox": [
    379.7,
    343.5,
    501.4,
    413.7
   ],
   "key": "p89-c47fe137"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e38",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "- Give cefalexin 500mg",
   "bbox": [
    385.4,
    412.9,
    478.9,
    423.7
   ],
   "key": "p89-6dd1b3bf"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e39",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "6 hourly or flucloxacillin 500mg 6 hourly for 5 days. - If severe penicillin allergy2,",
   "bbox": [
    385.4,
    422.9,
    489.7,
    453.7
   ],
   "key": "p89-4015fab0"
  },
  {
   "id": "p89-out-e40",
   "page": 89,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "give instead azithromycin 500mg daily for 3 days. • If intolerable or recurrent infections, arrange for excision once infection resolved.",
   "bbox": [
    379.7,
    452.9,
    498.7,
    503.7
   ],
   "key": "p89-705606c6"
  },
  {
